# Companion avatar height (HARD)

User-confirmed eye-to-eye at true **5′11″** on Galaxy XR (2026-08-24). Do not regress.

## Contract

| Context | Behavior |
|---------|----------|
| **Surface / Galaxy 2D** | `COMPANION_DESKTOP_AVATAR_SCALE` (1.05), `feetOffsetY = 0` |
| **Immersive VR/MR** | Scale to `COMPANION_AVATAR_TARGET_HEIGHT_M` (71×0.0254). Local `feetOffsetY = -minY×scale` so feet sit on floor. Entity locomotion Y stays `COMPANION_XR_FLOOR_Y` (0). |

## Forbidden regressions

- Measuring bbox with R3F `root.scale` still applied (under-scales → too short)
- Accepting empty first-frame skinned bbox and leaving desktop 1.05 forever in immersive
- Changing locomotion / entity Y to “fix” height (offset is **local** on the VRM primitive)
- Applying immersive height normalize on panel-2D

## Source of truth

`chat/app/src/lib/companion-avatar-scale.ts` (+ tests). Wired in `galatea.tsx` via `resolveCompanionAvatarPresentation` + measure retry (`COMPANION_AVATAR_MEASURE_MAX_ATTEMPTS`).

Log: `[galatea-avatar] immersive height { measuredHeightM, scale, feetOffsetY, targetHeightM }`.

## After `chat/app/src/` edits

`bash OpenNexus3DStudio/scripts/sync-companion-to-surface.sh` — hard-refresh existing OpenNexus 3D tab (no new browser tab).
